    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.surround\n\n### Description\n\nI want to add a custom surround for `cc`, but currently, if multiple keys are involved, the surround effect is already generated when the first `c` is pressed.\n\n```lua\nrequire(\"mini.surround\").setup({\n  custom_surroundings = {\n    [\"cc\"] = { -- cc means Css Calc\n      input = { \"calc(().-())\" },\n      output = { left = \"calc(\", right = \")\" },\n    },\n  }\n})\n```\n\nIn this case, `word` would become `cwordc`。\n\n",
