        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\n\nAlthough I see the appeal, it doesn't look like a good idea to implement. It will require one of the following:\n1. Explicitly confirm every surrounding id with extra key (like `<CR>`). This will not be the case for usability and backward compatibility reasons.\n2. Manually implement custom parsing of surrounding ids to determine if/when there is enough keys from the user to uniquely identify the surrounding. As in 'mini.clue' and Neovim's own mappings.\n\nAlthough 2) is doable, I personally don't think it is worth the complexity. Surrounding already is kind of verbose and opening the door for even more verbosity is questionable (`saiwcc` is almost like a word in some fictional language). Also, this particular feature design should be aligned with how 'mini.ai' handles its textobject ids, so will require adjusting it there as well.\n\nSo I am going to close this as \"not planned\" for now, but I'd like to note that it is a \"95% not planned; 5% - maybe (if there is a strong use case)\".",
